From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] package licences of vendored lz4, xxHash and robin_map

ext/drjit-core/ext/lz4/{lz4,xxhash}.c compile straight into libdrjit-core.so,
and ext/drjit-core/ext/robin_map's header-only hash map is compiled into
both libdrjit-core.so and the _drjit_ext Python extension, but the wheel
only ships drjit's own top-level LICENSE (confirmed against the released
PyPI wheel's dist-info/licenses/). lz4/xxHash are BSD-2-Clause (Yann
Collet) and robin_map is MIT (Tessil), both requiring their own copyright
notice to travel with binary redistributions.

pyproject.toml declares no `license-files`, so scikit-build-core falls
back to its own root-only `LICEN[CS]E*` glob and never reaches these two
vendored, nested LICENSE files that already exist in the tree (as git
submodules). Listing all three explicitly is enough: scikit-build-core
copies each listed path into dist-info/licenses/<same relative path>
unchanged (see build/wheel.py's `wheel_dirs["metadata"] / "licenses" / x`),
so this only adds files, it does not change how the existing top-level
LICENSE is packaged.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; same gap on every architecture upstream already ships, not riscv64-specific]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -14,6 +14,11 @@ dependencies = [
   "typing_extensions;python_version<\"3.11\""
 ]
 requires-python = ">=3.8"
+license-files = [
+    "LICENSE",
+    "ext/drjit-core/ext/lz4/LICENSE",
+    "ext/drjit-core/ext/robin_map/LICENSE",
+]
 authors = [
     { name = "Wenzel Jakob", email = "wenzel.jakob@epfl.ch" },
     { name = "Christian Döring", email = "christian.doering@tum.de" },
